sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as PublisherSpout
    participant B1 as BrokerBolt i<br/>(primary)
    participant B2 as BrokerBolt (i mod 10)+1<br/>(backup / watcher)
    participant FS as Shared state dir<br/>(/tmp/ebs-state/&lt;broker&gt;.json)

    Note over B1,B2: Ring topology: backup(i) = broker((i mod 10) + 1)<br/>broker1→broker2, …, broker10→broker1<br/>HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS = 1200 · HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MS = 5000

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
        Note over B1: maybeEmitHeartbeat() runs while processing publications
        loop every publication
            P->>B1: publication tuple
            B1->>B1: process & match subscriptions
            alt now - lastHeartbeatSentMs >= 1200 ms
                B1->>B1: lastHeartbeatSentMs = now<br/>seqNo = ++localSequence
                B1-->>B2: heartbeat_stream<br/>Heartbeat{source=brokerI,<br/>target=backup, timestamp, seqNo}
                Note over B1,B2: fieldsGrouping on target_broker<br/>routes to the backup task
                B2->>B2: handleHeartbeat()<br/>lastHeartbeat[brokerI] = timestamp
            else interval not elapsed
                B1->>B1: skip emit (throttled)
            end
        end
    end

    Note over B2: checkFailover() runs at the end of every execute()

    alt heartbeats keep arriving
        B2->>B2: now - lastHeartbeat[brokerI] <= 5000 ms<br/>primary considered ALIVE → no action
    else primary goes silent
        Note over B1: broker i crashes / simulatedDown<br/>→ stops emitting heartbeats
        B2->>B2: now - lastHeartbeat[brokerI] > 5000 ms<br/>and not already in failedPrimaries
        B2->>B2: failedPrimaries.add(brokerI)<br/>"activated failover for brokerI"
        B2->>FS: adoptPrimaryFromSnapshot(brokerI)<br/>loadSnapshotForBroker(brokerI)
        FS-->>B2: deliveredIds, localSubscriptions,<br/>pendingDeliveries
        B2->>B2: take over brokerI's subscriptions<br/>& replay pending deliveries
    end
